#====================================================================
# DRAFT-ohos-unsigned-elf-permission-denied - Unsigned ELF rejected by the OHOS loader
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-ohos-unsigned-elf-permission-denied
trigger_tool:           conan|cmake|ctest
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        Error loading shared library.*\(needed by.*\)|Error relocating.*symbol not found|Permission denied

severity:               2
category:               ohos|linking|packaging|conan|signing
match_keywords:         Error loading shared library, Permission denied, Error relocating, symbol not found, .codesign, unsigned, ELF signature, binary-sign-tool, selfSign, dlopen, ctypes.CDLL, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, signed-runtime, conan package, dependency binary
title:                  Unsigned dependency ELF makes the OHOS loader fail with "Permission denied"

root_cause:             The OHOS loader refuses to map an ELF that has no valid .codesign self-signature, and musl reports the refusal as "Error loading shared library <name>: Permission denied". The "-- Error relocating ... symbol not found" lines that follow are a second-order effect (the library was never mapped), not missing symbols; nm -D on the same file shows the symbols present. A Conan package binary pulled from the registry may carry an empty .codesign section (e.g. kcoreaddons5/5.116.0), so anything linking it fails before main().
verification_cmd:       python3 -c "import ctypes; ctypes.CDLL('<pkg>/lib/libX.so.N')"  # Permission denied => signature; not found => SONAME/path

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           sign-own-elfs-and-signed-runtime-copy
rec_description:        Distinguish with a single-file dlopen probe. In package(), sign the recipe's own ELFs (llvm-objcopy --remove-section .codesign, then binary-sign-tool sign -selfSign 1). For dependency libraries that are unsigned in the registry, do NOT modify the dependency package: shutil.copy2 the dependency lib/* into <build_folder>/signed-runtime (copy2 follows symlinks so each alias becomes a real file), sign each copy, and prepend that directory to LD_LIBRARY_PATH for upstream ctest and test_package. Apply the same to test_package consumers.
rec_command:            llvm-objcopy --remove-section .codesign <elf> && binary-sign-tool sign -inFile <elf> -outFile <tmp> -selfSign 1 && mv <tmp> <elf> && chmod 755 <elf>
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-layer|test-package

forbid_1_pattern:        Permission denied.*symbol not found|Error relocating.*symbol not found
forbid_1_reason:         Treating the "symbol not found" lines as the root cause leads to chasing non-existent symbol/link problems; the symbols are present and the real cause is the missing .codesign section.
forbid_1_consequence:    Hours lost on SONAME/symlink/RPATH hypotheses; the upstream test suite never runs.

forbid_2_pattern:        .*package_folder.*(chmod|copy2|sign|unlink)
forbid_2_reason:         Writing into a dependency's package folder mutates a shared conan cache entry (R49/E524: CI and local share the filesystem); sign a private copy under build_folder instead.
forbid_2_consequence:    Cache corruption that reproduces locally but not in CI (or vice versa).

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-ohos-unsigned-elf-permission-denied.md
last_updated:           2026-10-03
source_event:           kauth5/5.116.0 HarmonyOS PC local conan create (task: feat/kauth5-5.116.0)
draft:                  true
contributor_id:         AtomCode
authors:                AtomCode (deepseek-flash)
